# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# local/ - everything on this machine that is not part of the repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database exports, the credentials that go with them, rotated campaign logs,
# the Windows launchers and internal notes all live under local/, with an index
# in local/README.md. None of it is published; this rule is what keeps it that
# way. The rules further down still match those files by name and extension on
# their own, so a file that leaves local/ is still ignored.
local/

# Java / Maven
api/target/
*.class

# Node / Vite
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
npm-debug.log*

# Env overrides (commit .env.example, not .env)
.env

# Campaign send logs (bind-mounted from the api container) — operational data,
# and they contain recipient addresses.
logs/
# By name as well as by folder: rotated runs get archived to local/logs-archive/,
# and the rule above only ever matched them while they sat in logs/.
campaign-current*.log

# Local launchers and internal notes. Kept on disk because they are useful here,
# untracked because they are not part of what this repo publishes: the .bat files
# are Windows convenience wrappers around docker compose, and SAAS-MIGRATION.md is
# an internal assessment of work that has not been done.
*.bat
SAAS-MIGRATION.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No database contents in this repo. Ever.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo holds code, schema and infrastructure. It does not hold a copy of the
# data: the history was rewritten on 2026-08-22 to remove the dumps it used to
# carry, and these rules are what stop them coming back. Dumps are taken with
# a script that lives outside the checkout, along with its credentials.
#
# Deliberately broad, and deliberately by extension rather than by path: the
# failure this guards against is someone dropping a dump into a folder nobody
# thought to list. A migration under db/migration is the one legitimate .sql that
# is checked in, and it is not matched here because it is schema, not data.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.backup
db-backup-*/
db-export/
**/dumps/

# Connection strings pasted while setting up a hosted database. Their real home is
# .env, ignored above - this is here so a scratch file on the way there cannot be
# committed by accident. A password in git history is a password you have to rotate.
db/creds.txt
*creds*.txt
*.credentials

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
